  "question": {
    "text": "Let $[x]$ denote the greatest integer function, and let m and n respectively be the numbers of the points, where the function $f(x)=[x]+|x-2|,-2 \\lt x \\lt 3$, is not continuous and not differentiable. Then $\\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{n}$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "QE96Q",
      "text": "6",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "G7Zn7",
      "text": "8",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2hWYO",
      "text": "9",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "y05Ba",
      "text": "7",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& f(x)=[x]+|x-2|,-2 < x < 3 \\\\\n& \\therefore f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}\n-x,-2 < x < -1 \\\\\n1-x,-1 \\leq x < 0 \\\\\n2-x, 0 \\leq x < 1 \\\\\n3-x, 1 \\leq x < 2 \\\\\nx, 2 \\leq x < 3\n\\end{array}\\right.\n\\end{aligned}$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5K_XhL9qqwvZMjVbmbQCViT-bnkWlXG8yBSqjJbI4hs.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nIt is clearly discontinues at 4 points and nondifferentiable at 4 points.\n$\\therefore \\quad m+n=8$",
    "image": null
  },
